      "content": "okay, so you're saying the \"duty\" to protect secrets is the stronger legal position here. but wouldn't a prosecutor argue that using \"executive privilege\" as a blanket excuse to avoid answering for specific intelligence failures is just an abuse of power? it feels like there's a fine line between national security and just being unaccountable. in your view, does the law actually support using that kind of vague language to block an investigation?",
